---
import Card from "astro-theme-university/components/Card.astro";
import CardGrid from "astro-theme-university/components/CardGrid.astro";
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import heroImage from "../assets/images/hero-home.avif";
import { courseMeta } from "../course-config";
import { learningOutcomes } from "../learning-outcomes";
import { sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../site-config";

// STARTER_CONTENT: replace the hero artwork and its alt text below, then
// remove this comment.
---

<ContentLayout
  title={`${courseMeta.code}: ${courseMeta.title}`}
  description={courseMeta.description}
  heroImage={heroImage}
  heroImageAlt="A lecture theatre reduced to flat gold and black shapes, rows of seats sweeping past the frame, in a two-ink risograph print"
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <ul class="course-tags" aria-label="Course tags">
    {courseMeta.tags.map((tag) => <li>{tag}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <h2>What you will do</h2>
  <p>
    Each week you take one continuity technique apart, from the retcon to the
    soft reboot, using a specific film or episode as the case. Along the way you
    audit a failure in a franchise you know, write the repair for one it never
    fixed, and brief your seminar on a decision a studio made and the option it
    passed over.
  </p>
  <p>
    You leave with a continuity bible for a small universe of your own, tested
    by handing it to a stranger and fixing everything they got wrong.
  </p>

  <h2>Who it is for</h2>
  <p>
    First-year students from any degree. You need no prior study of film or
    television, and no loyalty to any of the three franchises. You do need to
    watch them: each {sessionLabels.singular.toLowerCase()} lists its set
    viewing under what to bring, and most weeks ask for one to four hours.
  </p>

  <h2>Learning outcomes</h2>
  <p>
    Upon successful completion, students will have the knowledge and skills to:
  </p>
  <ol class="outcomes">
    {
      learningOutcomes.map(({ verb, rest }) => (
        <li>
          <strong>{verb}</strong> {rest}
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ol>

  <h2>Where to go next</h2>
  <CardGrid columns={2}>
    <Card title={sessionLabels.plural} href="/sessions/">
      <p>One continuity technique a week, and what to bring to each.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Assessment" href="/assessments/">
      <p>What is marked, which outcomes it tests, and when it is due.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Lectures" href="/lectures/">
      <p>One lecture for each learning outcome, and the week 5 slides.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="People" href="/people/">
      <p>Who teaches the course, and who to ask first.</p>
    </Card>
  </CardGrid>
</ContentLayout>

<style>
  .course-tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-block: 0 2rem;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .outcomes li + li {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .course-tags li {
    padding: 0.25rem 0.65rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
    background: var(--at-bg-alt);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
</style>
